Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 16:10:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06950/11362] [outer-loop] Task 13: multiseed generator-size
 A/B resolves exp5596/5597 contradiction (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5598)

Operator directive: "scale up the roster and add multiple seeds." Ran all three arms together
(current Qwen3.5-9B-MTP, candidate_27b Qwen3.6-27B-MTP, candidate_35b_moe Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-MTP)
on a widened 4-game roster (m0r0, sk48, cd82, sp80) with 3 independent repeats per (arm, game)
cell (n=12 draws/arm), batching the loop by arm (one server per arm, reused across all its
draws, stopped once before the next arm starts) instead of exp5596/5597's interleaved
per-attempt restarts.

First attempt hit a genuine hardware fault: GPU 1 (the outer loop's eGPU-hosted RTX 3090) fell
completely off the PCI bus mid-run -- nvidia-smi -q -i 1 returned "No devices were found," and
even nvidia-smi --gpu-reset could not reach it. Required an operator power-cycle to recover.
Hardened the script before retrying: a per-arm n_ctx reduction for the 35B arm (modest --
manually confirmed the tight VRAM margin is dominated by model weights, not KV cache) and a
real fix -- a mid-run GPU-1-health check before every draw that aborts cleanly with a distinct
blocked_gpu1_lost_mid_run verdict if the GPU vanishes again, instead of silently falling back
to the slow iGPU mid-arm (what happened, undetected, in the first attempt).

The retry completed cleanly (no fault) and resolves the exp5596-vs-exp5597 contradiction: at
real statistical power, BOTH candidates beat the current generator. Mean heldout_accuracy:
current=0.100, candidate_27b=0.525, candidate_35b_moe=0.391. Paired win/loss/tie vs current:
candidate_27b 10-0-2 (near-unanimous, exp5596's positive finding replicates and strengthens);
candidate_35b_moe 5-1-5 (net positive but noisy, consistent with exp5597's single negative
draw having been an unlucky sample). honest_verdict:
generator_size_multiseed_ab_ranked_candidate_27b_gt_candidate_35b_moe_gt_current.

Frozen live-submission generator remains unchanged; candidate_27b's edge is now well-supported
enough to justify a genuine cost/benefit evaluation, still an explicit operator decision.

